00:26:07.370 --> 00:26:15.860
I can put us in a place we are familiar with
let's find the Lactase gene.

00:26:15.860 --> 00:26:25.480
Now I want to upload a track and this is a
track available here as one of the supported

00:26:25.480 --> 00:26:27.060
accession types.

00:26:27.060 --> 00:26:39.830
This is a SRA run for the library RP 11 which
comprises 70% of the genome sequence.

00:26:39.830 --> 00:26:44.610
Remember only one allele is included in the
reference assembly so it will be interesting

00:26:44.610 --> 00:26:47.500
to see what the other allele is this person
has.

00:26:47.500 --> 00:26:54.440
I will load that.

00:26:54.440 --> 00:26:59.570
The same kind of thing we saw before where
there are red places are the mismatches so

00:26:59.570 --> 00:27:04.250
there are places where this person is heterozygous
for positions in the lactase gene.

00:27:04.250 --> 00:27:12.450
We will do one last search and look for the
SNP that's responsible for, in some populations,

00:27:12.450 --> 00:27:16.650
the persistence of lactase activity in adulthood,
what provides people the ability to drink

00:27:16.650 --> 00:27:19.710
milk without gastrointestinal distress.

00:27:19.710 --> 00:27:27.350
I will go ahead and load that SNP to look
at the genotype at that position.

00:27:27.350 --> 00:27:32.610
Here is the SNP I am talking about.

00:27:32.610 --> 00:27:38.780
I will search instead of the gene which we
have been doing all day, I will search with

00:27:38.780 --> 00:27:41.799
this particular SNP.

00:27:41.799 --> 00:27:50.230
It lands me right here and I am in a different
gene, MCM6.

00:27:50.230 --> 00:27:55.350
All these SNPs landing in the promoter of
the lactase gene so it's upstream relatively

00:27:55.350 --> 00:27:56.720
speaking.

00:27:56.720 --> 00:28:05.860
You see this person is a heterozygote for
this change and has the A allele at this position

00:28:05.860 --> 00:28:09.830
that allows lactase to be expressed in adulthood.

00:28:09.830 --> 00:28:15.549
The G is the one in the genome assembly is
the most common allele worldwide is the one

00:28:15.549 --> 00:28:18.049
that is incorporated into this part of chromosome
2.

00:28:18.049 --> 00:28:24.780
And of course you can zoom out and see that
